      <memberdef kind="variable" id="struct_x_asu___key_manager_key_metadata_1a3063301d7a110770365f39d08f05f37b" prot="public" static="no" mutable="no">
        <type>u32</type>
        <definition>u32 XAsu_KeyManagerKeyMetadata::CompositeKeyId</definition>
        <argsstring></argsstring>
        <name>CompositeKeyId</name>
        <briefdescription>
<para><verbatim> Composite key identifier, built with
</verbatim> <ref refid="xasu__keymanagerinfo_8h_1ae004a9a17cd9a33a3c6f1281a7de3e77" kindref="member">XASU_KM_COMPOSE_KEY_ID()</ref>: </para>        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para><itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>Bits [31:24]: vault ID. Always required.</para></listitem><listitem><para>Bits [23:16]: key type, an XAsu_KeyManagerSubVaultType value. Required by the Store Key API, where it may be OR&apos;ed with XASU_KM_KEYTYPE_WRAPPED_BIT_MASK. On the Generate Key APIs, set the same key type the API uses: XASU_AES_SUBVAULT_ID, XASU_IV_SUBVAULT_ID or XASU_KDF_HMAC_SUBVAULT_ID, and for key pairs XASU_RSA_PVT_SUBVAULT_ID, XASU_ECC_PVT_SUBVAULT_ID, XASU_MLDSA_PVT_SUBVAULT_ID or XASU_MLKEM_PVT_SUBVAULT_ID.The returned key IDs carry the sub-vault type of each stored key.</para></listitem><listitem><para>Bits [15:0]: 1-based key slot within the sub-vault. 0 requests an auto-assigned slot; other values request a specific slot, which may be rejected if already in use. Key pair APIs apply the requested slot to both the private and public sub-vaults. </para></listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
